5TYPES OF ARTIFACT REPOSITORIES:  S3,S3,CODE ARTIFACT,S3,CODEBUILD 
==================================
1)PIPELINE ARTIFACT: ITS GETS THE CODE FROM CODE COMMIT WRPAS IT AS ZIP STORES IN S3 TEMPORARILY, AND PASSES IT BETWEEN EACH STAGE.
  DELETED AFTER THE PIPELINE RUN FINISHES.
2)BUILD ARTIFACT: BUILD ARTIFACT STORES THE BUILD OUTPUT FILES (JAR,WAR,ZIP). IT GOES TO S3 AND CODE DEPLPY PICK IT UP FROM S3 TO DEPLOY ONTO EC2. IT DOES NOT GO TO ARTIFACT AUTOMATICALLY
3)CODE ARTIFACT: CODE ARTIFACT STORES THE REQUIRED DEPENDENCIES PACKAGES THAT PROJECT DECLARES IN POM.XML OR PACKAGE.JSON. IT ACTS AS A PROXY TO MAVEN CENTRL OR NPM. SO CODE BUILD DOWNLOAD DEPENDENCIES THROUGH IT.
4)DEPLOYMENT ARTIFACT: DEPLOYMENT ARTIFACT IS THE FINAL BUNDLE THAT CODE DEPLOY ACTUALLY USES. ITS THE JAR FILE + APPSPEC.YML + SCRIPTD+FOLDER ALL ZIPPED TOGETHER. CODE DEPLOY NEEDS ALL THRE TOGHER TO KNOW WHERE TO COPY THE FILE AND WHICH SCRIPT TO TO RUN ON THE SERVER.
5)TEST REPORT ARIFACT: IT STORES THE TEST RESULTS(JUNIT,XML FILES) PRODUCED WHEN CODE BUILD RUNS OUR UNIT TESTS. IT DOES NOT GO TO S3.
  IT STORES TO DIRECTLY CODE BUILD REPORTS. WHERE WE SEE PASS (FAIL COUNTS,WHICH TESTS FAILED, AND TEST HOSTORIES OVERTIME INSIDE THE AWS CONSOLE)


